criteria:
Inclusion criteria:
1. Participant is willing and able to give informed consent for participation in the study, in accordance with Ethics Committee guidance;
2. Age ≥18 years, male or female;
3. Diagnosis of ESKD, regardless of underlying cause, with either: (a) current maintenance dialysis (haemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis), or (b) chronic kidney disease with eGFR <15 mL/min/1.73 m² calculated using the CKD-EPI equation;
4. Scheduled to receive a deceased donor kidney transplant — either from a DBD donor or a DCD donor — with surgery expected to occur within the next 24 hours.
Exclusion criteria:
1. Previous enrolment and randomisation into this study;
2. Pregnancy or current breastfeeding.
3. Current enrolment in an interventional clinical trial involving an investigational medicinal product that could interfere with the study endpoints or participant safety, as judged by the PI;
4. Not expected to survive beyond 24 hours;
5. Scheduled for a living donor kidney transplant, unless this is cancelled in favour of a transplant from a deceased donor;
6. Scheduled for a multi-organ transplant (recipients of dual or en-bloc kidney transplants are not excluded);
7. Documented congenital error of amino acid metabolism;
8. Documented contraindication to AA infusion as per SmPC;
9. Documented hypersensitivity (known allergy) to one or more components of Aminoven 10%;
10. Severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh score >7 points);
